  "clock_bounds_propagation": [
    "ClockBounds::hsi/external/rtc_source retain their existing qualification; PLL-only multiplied_by sets rate_only and keeps the exact divisor.",
    "ClockBounds::divided_by uses struct update, preserving rate_only.",
    "Clocks stores source and optional raw PLL bounds; sys/hclk/pclk getters return/divide those exact bounds. hsi_bounds remains factory-HSI independently.",
    "central RCC bus_clock_bounds and kernel_clock_bounds use the frozen Clocks bounds, not nominal Hertz; peripheral-local division preserves the flag.",
    "Classic ADC Config::timing rejects before both blocking/async constructors acquire/reset/write the peripheral; configuration and channel timing share that path.",
    "AUTOTRIM counter uses raw HSIOSC/HSE/LSI/LSE and cannot select PLL. L083 complementary PWM is not qualified in the baseline.",
    "RTC window loop uses its rate-derived delay only as an interval between actual WINDOW observations. No strict deadline is inferred.",
    "AWT is absent from L083; its existing validate() constructs ClockBounds::hsi(1) followed by its raw-HSI prescaler on other families, never selected SYSCLK/PLL.",
    "LPTIM::enable uses HCLK/PCLK endpoint ratio to wait two counter ticks, not an absolute-nanosecond promise. Both clocks share the frozen PLL with integer downstream divisors (U083 PDF236/238, printed235/237).",
    "TimeDriver::validate_clock uses the exact nominal numerator/denominator, and init stores pclk_bounds.divided_by(divisor); its blackout obligation remains fewer than32768 actual ticks for rate-only PLL.",
    "Timer counter/PWM/QEI/trigger, Halltim and LPTIM bounds copy central RCC envelopes or divide them; SPI stores/divides the exact kernel bounds; I2C uses endpoints for rate bounds, not strict duration helpers."
  ],
  "public_api_caveats": [
    "Additive L083-only Config.pll, Sysclk::PLL, Pll/PllSource/PllMul, Clocks.pll_bounds/pll_frequency. New enum variants affect exhaustive matches.",
    "ClockBounds has_cycle_timing_bounds is additive. Existing duration method signatures and old-source behavior remain; new PLL source explicitly panics for unsupported strict duration helpers.",
    "L083 ADC checked constructors reject PLL with UnqualifiedCycleTiming before hardware writes. No existing HSI/HSE configuration is newly rejected.",
    "Direct PAC PLL source/ranges/multiplier/wait/debug fields become typed and PLL.STABLE loses its setter. Raw-PAC callers must adapt; exact offsets/widths preserved except own-manual reserved-debug field addition.",
